__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.env
.DS_Store
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Course materials are copyright UCT / the course convener — never commit them.
corpus/raw/*
!corpus/raw/README.md
# The manifest is a permission trail, not course content. It must survive.
!corpus/raw/MANIFEST.md
corpus/processed/*
!corpus/processed/.gitkeep

# Run outputs were assumed regenerable. For the frontier arm they are not: the
# five C0 runs cost real money, and they target model versions that expire —
# gemini-3.1-pro-preview is a preview, gemini-2.5-pro shuts down 2026-10-16,
# and gpt-5.6-sol will be superseded. Rerunning next term would not reproduce
# them, it would measure different models. So ungrounded runs are committed.
#
# Grounded runs are NOT, and this is a copyright rule rather than a size one.
# A C2 answer is instructed to ground every claim in the retrieved passages, so
# it quotes UCT course notes at length. This repository is public, and the
# convener's permission does not extend to republishing the material. Review a
# grounded run by hand before ever adding it.
runs/*
!runs/.gitkeep
!runs/*-C0-*
!runs/*-C1-*
# Dry runs produce fake answers and must never be mistaken for evidence. They
# are not distinguishable from real runs by directory name - only manifest.json
# says dry_run - so `git add -A` will happily commit one. Delete dry-run
# directories rather than relying on a rule that cannot see inside them; the
# pre-commit check below is the reminder:
#   grep -l '"dry_run": true' runs/*/manifest.json
